ll script structure:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"docstring\"\"\"\n\nimport json, os, re, shutil, subprocess, sys, tempfile\n\ndef find_repo_root(start_file): ...\ndef read_text(path): ...\ndef list_go_files(dirpath): ...\ndef concat_files(paths): ...\ndef run(cmd, cwd, timeout=300, env=None): ...\ndef tail(text, n=1200): ...\n\ndef main():\n    errors = []\n    repo_root = find_repo_root(__file__)\n    go = shutil.which('go')\n    if not go: ...\n\n    internal_dir = os.path.join(repo_root, 'internal')\n    builder_dir = os.path.join(internal_dir, 'builder')\n    prompt_dir = os.path.join(internal_dir, 'prompt')\n    templates_dir = os.path.join(prompt_dir, 'templates')\n\n    # ---- Test 1: 正常路径 go build ----\n    build_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task5_build_')\n    build_out = os.path.join(build_dir, 'rick')\n    rc, out, err = run([go, 'build', '-o', build_out, './cmd/rick'], cwd=repo_root, timeout=300)\n    if rc != 0: errors.append('go build ./cmd/rick failed:\\n' + tail(err or out))\n    elif not os.path.isfile(build_out): errors.append(...)\n\n    # ---- Test 1: go test ./internal/builder/... ./internal/prompt/... ----\n    rc, out, err = run([go, 'test', '-timeout', '180s', './internal/builder/...', './internal/prompt/...', '-v'], cwd=repo_root, timeout=240)\n    if rc != 0: errors.append('go test ./internal/builder/... ./internal/prompt/... failed:\\n' + tail(err or out))\n\n    # ---- Test 2 (边界): templates 零改动 ----\n    rc, out, err = run(['git', 'diff', '--stat', '--', 'internal/prompt/templates/'], cwd=repo_root, timeout=60)\n    if rc != 0: errors.append(...)\n    elif out.strip(): errors.append('templates changed (unstaged):\\n' + tail(out))\n    rc2, out2, err2 = run(['git', 'diff', '--cached', '--stat', '--', 'internal/prompt/templates/'], ...)\n    if rc2 != 0 or out2.strip(): errors.append(...)\n\n    # ---- Test 2 (边界): dry-run 注入路径 ----\n    if os.path.isfile(build_out):\n        rc, out, err = run([build_out, 'plan', '--dry-run'], cwd=repo_root, timeout=120)\n        if rc != 0: errors.append('rick plan --dry-run failed:\\n' + tail(err or out))\n        else:\n            # grep -cE\n            # use Python regex count on stdout lines instead of shell grep\n            pattern = re.compile(r'plan/task|doing/debug|/jobs/|/domain')\n            matches = [line for line in out.splitlines() if pattern.search(line)]\n            if len(matches) < 1:\n                errors.append('rick plan --dry-run output missing injected path fragments (plan/task|doing/debug|/jobs/|/domain)')\n    else:\n        # build already failed; skip dry-run (already recorded)\n        pass\n\n    # ---- Test 3 (异常): PIBuilder.BuildPlan(\"\") ----\n    rc, out, err, msg = check_pibuilder_empty(repo_root, go)\n    if msg: errors.append(msg)\n\n    # ---- 结构检查 (KR) ----\n    ...\n\n    result = {...}\n    print(json.dumps(result))\n    sys.exit(...)\n```\n\nWait, for the dry-run test, I need to use the built binary. But the build output goes to a temp dir. Actually I'll build to `bin/rick` as the spec says? The spec says `go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick`. Hmm. But writing to `bin/rick` modifies the working tree (bin/rick is git-tracked and currently has uncommitted changes). That would make the test non-idempotent and pollute git status.\n\nThe task4.py test built to a temp dir: `build_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task4_build_')`. I'll do the same for task5 — build to temp dir. This keeps things clean. The spec's `-o bin/rick` is just an example of \"build succeeds\"; building to temp is equivalent and cleaner.\n\nActually wait, but the dry-run grep test in the spec says `./bin/rick plan --dry-run`. If I build to temp, I use my temp binary. That's fine and actually MORE correct (fresh build). I'll build to temp and use that binary for dry-run.\n\nLet me make sure the dry-run binary uses cwd=repo_root so GetRickDir resolves correctly. Yes.\n\nNow, about the grep: I'll use Python regex instead of shelling