ng/debug|/jobs/|/domain'`, expect ≥1. The `doing/debug` part is there presumably because the author intended to also check doing dry-run but only wrote plan.\n\nGiven the ambiguity, I should follow the test method LITERALLY (plan --dry-run + grep ≥1). This is safe because:\n- Currently: matches 5 lines (≥1) → passes (but this is OK, it's not the RED signal).\n- After refactor: should still match ≥1 (via plan/task, /jobs/, /domain).\n\nBut wait — I want to make sure the test actually MEANINGFULLY verifies \"注入路径\" (path injection). The note emphasizes that `task_info_section`/`debug_context` become real path fragments. Since those are doing-template vars, maybe I should ALSO run `rick doing --dry-run` to check `doing/debug` appears.\n\nLet me check what `rick doing --dry-run` does currently, and whether it's feasible to run (it might need a job with plan/tasks).\n\nActually, let me look at `runDoingDryRun` in doing.go."}}
